# testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime: a closure whose loan is left to the stub of a call by value stands in the heap too. The stub hands a callee whose word does not borrow a copy, so what is overwritten behind the call is held by nobody who may hold it.
# The lie, testing=NoCalleeKeepsWhatItIsHanded: the word of keeps() says that it borrows its first argument.
